#: bin/Machin:33
msgid ""
"Usage: Machin [--config FILE] BINARY [OPTIONS…]  or  Machin "
"logs|dev|dev-test|dev-screenshots\n"
"Binaries: %s. Full help: Machin --help\n"
msgstr ""
"Usage : Machin [--config FICHIER] BINAIRE [OPTIONS…]  ou  Machin "
"logs|dev|dev-test|dev-screenshots\n"
"Binaires : %s. Aide complète : Machin --help\n"

#: bin/Machin:39
msgid ""
"Machin — single command to reach the MachinCast binaries.\n"
"\n"
"Usage:\n"
"  Machin [--config FILE] BINARY [OPTIONS…]\n"
"  Machin logs [journalctl OPTIONS…]\n"
"  Machin dev | dev-test | dev-screenshots [DIRECTORY]\n"
"  Machin -h | --help | --binaries\n"
"\n"
"Binaries (Machin BINARY calls Machin_BINARY with the options that follow,\n"
"taken from the .venv venv of the project, without it being activated, or "
"else from the PATH):\n"
"  player       on-air broadcast, normally launched as a systemd service\n"
"  indexer      check of the sound files and update of the database\n"
"  interface    graphical programming interface\n"
"  maintenance-db\n"
"               backs up, checks and optimises the database\n"
"               (https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/issues/127)\n"
"  purge        erases from the database what exceeds the expiry duration: "
"old\n"
"               plays of the airplay, lines of the log, deleted elements; "
"never a\n"
"               file (https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/issues/268)\n"
"\n"
"  Help of a binary: Machin BINARY --help\n"
"\n"
"Following the logs:\n"
"  logs         follows live the log of the %s service (journalctl "
"--follow).\n"
"               The options that follow are passed to journalctl, for "
"instance:\n"
"               Machin logs --since \"1 hour ago\" --priority=warning\n"
"               Reading this log requires belonging to the adm or "
"systemd-journal group:\n"
"               install.sh adds the account that installs it.\n"
"\n"
"Development (computer installed by ./install.sh --dev):\n"
"  dev          opens a subshell in the MachinCast directory, venv "
"activated, with\n"
"               the prompt “(MachinCast dev)”; exit leaves it\n"
"  dev-test     runs ruff check, ruff format --check, mypy --strict, "
"shellcheck, pytest\n"
"               then bats, all even after a failure, with the tools of the "
"venv without it\n"
"               being activated; shows a summary per tool and ends in "
"failure if one\n"
"               of them fails. A missing tool is reported: ./install.sh "
"--dev installs it.\n"
"  dev-screenshots redoes the screenshots of the on-air guide, in "
"doc/fr/captures\n"
"               or in DIRECTORY: the interface off screen, on a "
"demonstration\n"
"               written in the test database, never in the production one.\n"
"\n"
"Wrapper options:\n"
"  --config FILE, --config=FILE\n"
"               TOML configuration file passed to the binary\n"
"               (by default, the binary reads machincast.toml in the "
"MachinCast directory:\n"
"               %s/machincast.toml)\n"
"  -h           minimal help\n"
"  --help       this full help\n"
"  --binaries   list of the binaries, one per line (used by the "
"autocompletion)\n"
"\n"
"Examples:\n"
"  Machin player --config essai.toml\n"
"  Machin indexer --help\n"
"  Machin logs\n"
"  Machin dev-test\n"
"\n"
"Exit codes:\n"
"  the one of the called binary, of journalctl for logs, or of the subshell "
"for dev;\n"
"  1            dev-test: at least one tool failed or is missing;\n"
"  %s            incorrect call of the wrapper (unknown binary or option);\n"
"  %s          binary, journalctl or venv not found.\n"
"\n"
"Documentation: "
"https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/blob/main/doc/fr/spec.md#7-wrapper-machin\n"
msgstr ""
"Machin — commande unique d'accès aux binaires de MachinCast.\n"
"\n"
"Usage :\n"
"  Machin [--config FICHIER] BINAIRE [OPTIONS…]\n"
"  Machin logs [OPTIONS DE journalctl…]\n"
"  Machin dev | dev-test | dev-screenshots [REPERTOIRE]\n"
"  Machin -h | --help | --binaries\n"
"\n"
"Binaires (Machin BINAIRE appelle Machin_BINAIRE avec les options qui "
"suivent,\n"
"pris dans le venv .venv du projet, sans qu'il soit activé, ou à défaut dans "
"le PATH) :\n"
"  player       diffusion de l'antenne, normalement lancée comme service "
"systemd\n"
"  indexer      vérification des fichiers sonores et mise à jour de la base\n"
"  interface    interface graphique de programmation\n"
"  maintenance-db\n"
"               sauvegarde, vérifie et optimise la base de données\n"
"               (https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/issues/127)\n"
"  purge        efface de la base ce qui dépasse la durée de péremption : "
"vieux\n"
"               passages de l'airplay, lignes du log, éléments supprimés ; "
"jamais un\n"
"               fichier "
"(https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/issues/268)\n"
"\n"
"  Aide d'un binaire : Machin BINAIRE --help\n"
"\n"
"Suivi des logs :\n"
"  logs         suit en direct le journal du service %s (journalctl "
"--follow).\n"
"               Les options qui suivent sont transmises à journalctl, par "
"exemple :\n"
"               Machin logs --since \"1 hour ago\" --priority=warning\n"
"               Lire ce journal demande d'appartenir au groupe adm ou "
"systemd-journal :\n"
"               install.sh y ajoute le compte qui l'installe.\n"
"\n"
"Développement (poste installé par ./install.sh --dev) :\n"
"  dev          ouvre un sous-shell dans le répertoire de MachinCast, venv "
"activé, avec\n"
"               l'invite « (MachinCast dev) » ; exit en sort\n"
"  dev-test     lance ruff check, ruff format --check, mypy --strict, "
"shellcheck, pytest\n"
"               puis bats, tous même après un échec, avec les outils du venv "
"sans qu'il\n"
"               soit activé ; affiche un bilan par outil et se termine en "
"échec si l'un\n"
"               d'eux échoue. Un outil absent se signale : ./install.sh "
"--dev l'installe.\n"
"  dev-screenshots refait les captures d'écran du guide de l'antenne, dans "
"doc/fr/captures\n"
"               ou dans REPERTOIRE : l'interface hors de l'écran, sur une "
"démonstration\n"
"               écrite dans la base de test, jamais dans celle de "
"production.\n"
"\n"
"Options du wrapper :\n"
"  --config FICHIER, --config=FICHIER\n"
"               fichier de configuration TOML transmis au binaire\n"
"               (par défaut, le binaire lit machincast.toml dans le "
"répertoire de MachinCast :\n"
"               %s/machincast.toml)\n"
"  -h           aide minimale\n"
"  --help       cette aide complète\n"
"  --binaries   liste des binaires, un par ligne (utilisée par "
"l'autocomplétion)\n"
"\n"
"Exemples :\n"
"  Machin player --config essai.toml\n"
"  Machin indexer --help\n"
"  Machin logs\n"
"  Machin dev-test\n"
"\n"
"Codes de sortie :\n"
"  celui du binaire appelé, de journalctl pour logs, ou du sous-shell pour "
"dev ;\n"
"  1            dev-test : au moins un outil en échec ou absent ;\n"
"  %s            appel incorrect du wrapper (binaire ou option inconnus) ;\n"
"  %s          binaire, journalctl ou venv introuvable.\n"
"\n"
"Documentation : "
"https://github.com/dascritch/machincast/blob/main/doc/fr/spec.md#7-wrapper-machin\n"

